# Master prompt for building the project

You can give the following prompt to a coding agent such as Cursor, Claude Code, or another coding model:

```text
You are a senior full-stack AI engineer.

Build a production-quality MVP called:

"AI Book Universe"

The application is an AI-powered book discovery and knowledge platform.

The core idea is:

Users upload books.
Each book is processed into pages, chapters and chunks.
Chunks are embedded and stored in PostgreSQL + pgvector.
A book-level semantic embedding is generated.
The book embedding is reduced to XYZ coordinates using UMAP.
Three.js renders every book as a point in a 3D semantic universe.

When a user clicks a point, they should see:
- Book cover
- Title
- Author
- Description
- AI-generated short summary
- Detailed summary
- Topics
- Audience
- Chapter list
- Similar books
- Ask AI button
- Open book button

The user can ask questions about the selected book.
The RAG system retrieves relevant chunks from that specific book,
passes them to the LLM, and returns an answer with page/chapter citations.

Use LangChain for LLM/RAG functionality.
Use LangGraph for the RAG workflow.
Use Langfuse for LLM/RAG observability.

