==================================================
BOOK INGESTION
==================================================

Implement this pipeline:

PDF upload
    ↓
Create books record
    ↓
Extract PDF text page by page
    ↓
Preserve original page numbers
    ↓
Detect chapters where possible
    ↓
Create chunks
    ↓
Generate chunk embeddings
    ↓
Store chunks + embeddings
    ↓
Generate chapter summaries
    ↓
Generate book summary
    ↓
Generate book-level embedding
    ↓
Generate UMAP XYZ
    ↓
Store XYZ
    ↓
Mark book COMPLETED

The upload API must return immediately with:

bookId
status = PROCESSING

Processing should happen asynchronously.

Do not block the HTTP request while processing a large book.

Implement a worker/service abstraction so that the processing pipeline can later be moved to Redis/BullMQ/Azure Queue without redesigning the application.

==================================================
CHUNKING
==================================================

Implement a sensible recursive text splitter.

Chunk size should be configurable.

Use overlap.

Preserve:
- book_id
- chapter_id
- page_start
- page_end
- chunk_number

Do not lose page information.

Chunks may span multiple pages.

==================================================
EMBEDDINGS
==================================================

Generate embeddings for every chunk.

Store embeddings in:

book_chunks.embedding

Generate a book-level embedding separately.

Do NOT send the entire raw book into a single LLM prompt.

Use hierarchical aggregation.

Preferred:

chunks
 ↓
chapter representation
 ↓
book representation

A simple initial implementation can use normalized mean pooling.

Make the aggregation logic isolated so it can later be replaced by weighted pooling.

==================================================
BOOK SUMMARY
==================================================

Use hierarchical summarization.

Chunk/section summaries
        ↓
Chapter summaries
        ↓
Book summary

Generate:

1. short_summary
2. detailed_summary
3. audience
4. themes
5. key_takeaways

Store the result in book_summaries.

Do not regenerate the summary every time the user clicks a book.

Generate it during ingestion.

==================================================
3D SEMANTIC SPACE
==================================================

The full book content contributes to the book-level embedding.

Use the book-level embedding to calculate 3D coordinates.

Use UMAP.

Input:

N books × embedding dimensions

Output:

N books × 3 dimensions

Store:

position_x
position_y
position_z

IMPORTANT:

XYZ axes do not have predefined human meanings.

Do not label:
X = AI
Y = Programming
Z = Mathematics

Instead, explain that the coordinates represent a reduced semantic space.

Similar books should generally appear near each other.

Implement a Universe service:

getAllBookCoordinates()

Return:

id
title
author
cover_url
x
y
z

For a stable universe, fit UMAP on the existing collection and use transform for new books when possible.

Periodically rebuild the projection when the library changes significantly.

